[{:db/id "q-76356/selection/8d6be7ccdfa71acef62161e7a516764f568cbfedccab8fd5f32349336be31257" :answer/id #uuid "913d9f7a-6be6-5ce5-bc9b-0838e6187a30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76356/selection/69790fe34ed3ca2feeaa752e186fbd72c7454793fdd42454defcc97fbd5d3090" :answer/id #uuid "b6256f5c-3019-58fb-b53b-b7119ae5ddfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}-t)\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76356/selection/c2fa14ec4c218647d5ee6969fc233e70b130d03f13792d5b49594bd4fa0b43fc" :answer/id #uuid "35a1e638-1130-5f5f-b4c4-f64e542b468c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76356/selection/1166211c0371e8db5d5935d61a53ac528e1cad34dff3347a6835a3981f6cc1b9" :answer/id #uuid "dae89a72-1600-54e4-9c84-031c362442f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76356/selection/1bed8f70825392c552c26e8b32e617b5e5d54132eca900679c5b42ccc2294f85" :answer/id #uuid "0e32f329-f7fe-54eb-9e25-f974c51a5bda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76356/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0104e6b-d299-570c-9321-9dd31fe0dc97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76356/selection/1bed8f70825392c552c26e8b32e617b5e5d54132eca900679c5b42ccc2294f85" :answer-field/choices ["q-76356/selection/8d6be7ccdfa71acef62161e7a516764f568cbfedccab8fd5f32349336be31257" "q-76356/selection/69790fe34ed3ca2feeaa752e186fbd72c7454793fdd42454defcc97fbd5d3090" "q-76356/selection/c2fa14ec4c218647d5ee6969fc233e70b130d03f13792d5b49594bd4fa0b43fc" "q-76356/selection/1166211c0371e8db5d5935d61a53ac528e1cad34dff3347a6835a3981f6cc1b9" "q-76356/selection/1bed8f70825392c552c26e8b32e617b5e5d54132eca900679c5b42ccc2294f85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76356" :question/id #uuid "9dd51c2a-c921-500f-b456-d9efa51cbc02" :question/math-academy-id "q-76356" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+1,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+1,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}+1,$ $y={t}^{2}-1,$ and $z={t}^{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+2t\\,j+2t\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}|t| \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t>0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =({t}^{2}+1)+({t}^{2}-1)-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-{t}^{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}t\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76356/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28f7479a-a84c-59fa-a7ea-9377c7e65b19"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76356"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134201 :question/answer-fields 17592186131648] {:db/id "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/5986a0b840ea41d4ae1fd87a199ffbf96b5047dcc7ab95ba9018f7ef6cf19ea9" :answer/id #uuid "db6abd37-511e-57f2-9932-a3b496ea5c26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/fbe3c160dc0b9d44e501932ec16c6c772ce03d61cbe6afaaa8e52bd54abbaa2a" :answer/id #uuid "a77990c5-fe8c-527e-9e76-94b472837d77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/622ee9b27771fd991ba2cde4a6e8060941ee20583fe8a3048825696002e7b186" :answer/id #uuid "8b5d7bff-8f1f-526c-b103-10e5516f316c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/994f1fd3d77dfe32f908c3bbb83fb79e75d288f8db30cd41cfb1b723c24625c8" :answer/id #uuid "1c94b707-c28b-559a-b5bc-e382fd180353" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/afd492545f444bd1b183039227ea3d80ede5456364e78947c872a265c7407c4d" :answer/id #uuid "41c93104-a2cb-5d59-a2e2-1a9a032e6702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f149a362-a250-5474-b249-86f0f4f90145" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/fbe3c160dc0b9d44e501932ec16c6c772ce03d61cbe6afaaa8e52bd54abbaa2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/5986a0b840ea41d4ae1fd87a199ffbf96b5047dcc7ab95ba9018f7ef6cf19ea9" "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/fbe3c160dc0b9d44e501932ec16c6c772ce03d61cbe6afaaa8e52bd54abbaa2a" "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/622ee9b27771fd991ba2cde4a6e8060941ee20583fe8a3048825696002e7b186" "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/994f1fd3d77dfe32f908c3bbb83fb79e75d288f8db30cd41cfb1b723c24625c8" "q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1/afd492545f444bd1b183039227ea3d80ede5456364e78947c872a265c7407c4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40253"] :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2}(x-y)$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized \n by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{2}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}+t,$ and $y={t}^{2}-t.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)j \\\\  & =(2t+1)\\,i+(2t-1)\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t+1)^{2}+(2t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+4t+1+4{t}^{2}-4t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2}(x-y)$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\sqrt{2}[({t}^{2}+t)-({t}^{2}-t)] \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}2\\sqrt{2}t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40253/selection/ma-v1/3242ea41fcf275b7328f2ba66ffc057cee89f8e2cc9fa0145b921d3b91f468e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-76379/selection/61a082ab199a294a8f352375e101bbc6370e87ee4454dec32405c37040bd63b8" :answer/id #uuid "f64efa41-6263-59a9-a6f1-b44981e4a721" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76379/selection/d2464a30e3364452125c9bf88ab0b66735068c58a6da88e2b0707c987db3f0e1" :answer/id #uuid "5b6027e6-38d5-576d-99ba-3f4da765f197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76379/selection/ea7cd6e6d7b3b3bd894c7dfc75c4bd7f236dcdb933c1b39c657e61df91b4f83d" :answer/id #uuid "a466ee1a-0636-5ef1-943d-9604ed93d477" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76379/selection/549b080d9e6fd99799f5c80e60b79126ddb63648f832956f270237ba33511d59" :answer/id #uuid "2efaf384-28f6-5f87-8684-a7b4158bf923" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76379/selection/2873d95c2005da6a30f3b21f8e259e3f52ac83164615d98a5a465b976c140f09" :answer/id #uuid "63c1118f-0189-581b-9fda-c4dabf25030e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76379/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8559b7a4-0c32-5a71-a147-4bf4c6eaef11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76379/selection/549b080d9e6fd99799f5c80e60b79126ddb63648f832956f270237ba33511d59" :answer-field/choices ["q-76379/selection/61a082ab199a294a8f352375e101bbc6370e87ee4454dec32405c37040bd63b8" "q-76379/selection/d2464a30e3364452125c9bf88ab0b66735068c58a6da88e2b0707c987db3f0e1" "q-76379/selection/ea7cd6e6d7b3b3bd894c7dfc75c4bd7f236dcdb933c1b39c657e61df91b4f83d" "q-76379/selection/549b080d9e6fd99799f5c80e60b79126ddb63648f832956f270237ba33511d59" "q-76379/selection/2873d95c2005da6a30f3b21f8e259e3f52ac83164615d98a5a465b976c140f09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76379" :question/id #uuid "cfad2296-6fbf-598f-a4ed-63e51e9c1622" :question/math-academy-id "q-76379" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k$ for $\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k,$ then along the curve we have $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ and $z=t.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, if $f(x,y,z)=z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t((\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}) \\\\  & =t({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76379/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28f7479a-a84c-59fa-a7ea-9377c7e65b19"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76379"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167608/selection/f39edd8aff966dfc1baa5c0237355039b7ecfa3710dc13569f5f673295088ac0" :answer/id #uuid "c43ed53d-5f10-5ff3-bb1d-8dd752fc9e03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167608/selection/938ce8d9a42ab2fd2c44453c3c4687a1905805e1d7663586104b783e15c2f964" :answer/id #uuid "db7e534d-0de3-5758-9446-84e143bd5fa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{t}^{2}}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167608/selection/ef2a39f36f65f220f078e92c11e39fc412d0816551eff948867e6a0d409d7a8d" :answer/id #uuid "87b20329-b052-5fc3-acb3-c794774ad104" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t(2t+1)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167608/selection/bc150bd0b4862a8939198432ce3e1417472aff75f2b46928088fa02ef824b28c" :answer/id #uuid "3f425ffb-9c58-54c8-a367-48b7c55e320a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167608/selection/543ef51160a2f77fc032c6b81ae0e7f23f76ac5f8c09c053791c5e9ab06b175a" :answer/id #uuid "3a81142e-c1b3-5d63-b21a-fc1bc43cc0fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167608/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb16a510-45b5-596b-9fc3-365853a9af1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-167608/selection/543ef51160a2f77fc032c6b81ae0e7f23f76ac5f8c09c053791c5e9ab06b175a" :answer-field/choices ["q-167608/selection/f39edd8aff966dfc1baa5c0237355039b7ecfa3710dc13569f5f673295088ac0" "q-167608/selection/938ce8d9a42ab2fd2c44453c3c4687a1905805e1d7663586104b783e15c2f964" "q-167608/selection/ef2a39f36f65f220f078e92c11e39fc412d0816551eff948867e6a0d409d7a8d" "q-167608/selection/bc150bd0b4862a8939198432ce3e1417472aff75f2b46928088fa02ef824b28c" "q-167608/selection/543ef51160a2f77fc032c6b81ae0e7f23f76ac5f8c09c053791c5e9ab06b175a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167608" :question/id #uuid "536ee23d-4379-5a20-a2d1-8d734aa76c83" :question/math-academy-id "q-167608" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $0\\le t\\le 1?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{4y+1}$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-167608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28f7479a-a84c-59fa-a7ea-9377c7e65b19"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76377/selection/59b9dbad2935d4fd60bd94deac62c3b7ce221d9bfe245ead8a27282f4374acea" :answer/id #uuid "9e8fcd67-42a6-581d-b258-3ad822f7c3e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76377/selection/7121fd05b10a864238c523615e086ed3e822de9ed2327327480a1432d40649f3" :answer/id #uuid "d51e09f7-f9e7-52d8-a1ca-492510e13077" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}-2t)\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76377/selection/bc80c9527023fff26935d4be08d682f723003ef2c08149c45b54e994233a0787" :answer/id #uuid "e94321fd-5aa6-56ea-9920-7f84e085237b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{3}t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76377/selection/eed77b5da5e90fc65b60201bbf33b72ecdab020a831a61aebf0b38e6d5852d42" :answer/id #uuid "ea5daa05-c12a-5f99-abe5-c33c7680850f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+2t-1)\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76377/selection/5d8b547aac5b761669c6491a60cb5d8d511631d1eb2650fa7b2109eddeac5725" :answer/id #uuid "c21e9084-4f17-5ef5-a84a-e5fe774aaf49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+2t)\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76377/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd7ee32-007d-5095-a527-1f3bf508b06c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76377/selection/59b9dbad2935d4fd60bd94deac62c3b7ce221d9bfe245ead8a27282f4374acea" :answer-field/choices ["q-76377/selection/59b9dbad2935d4fd60bd94deac62c3b7ce221d9bfe245ead8a27282f4374acea" "q-76377/selection/7121fd05b10a864238c523615e086ed3e822de9ed2327327480a1432d40649f3" "q-76377/selection/bc80c9527023fff26935d4be08d682f723003ef2c08149c45b54e994233a0787" "q-76377/selection/eed77b5da5e90fc65b60201bbf33b72ecdab020a831a61aebf0b38e6d5852d42" "q-76377/selection/5d8b547aac5b761669c6491a60cb5d8d511631d1eb2650fa7b2109eddeac5725"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76377" :question/id #uuid "ab3f9fa8-df92-55e7-af2b-aaa7f2b53b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-76377" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $f(x,y,z)=2x-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1,\\,t+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1,\\,t+1⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2},$ $y=t-1,$ and $z=t+1.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=2x-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2({t}^{2})-(t-1)^{2}-(t+1)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-({t}^{2}-2t+1)-({t}^{2}+2t+1) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-{t}^{2}+2t-1-{t}^{2}-2t-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{2(2{t}^{2}+1)}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76377/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28f7479a-a84c-59fa-a7ea-9377c7e65b19"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76377"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167609/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "88f4b64c-0637-5605-afea-a3f0f66a6587" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167609/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "daf4dd48-8286-5ef4-9397-e5e3709a050e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167609/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "cef1b1ec-6f32-566c-9b29-3059b9bcc304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167609/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "3045b749-b61d-5b6c-99ec-e8a3e181cdf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167609/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "7b418321-4236-5f77-b8ef-cb865101686d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167609/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4b5fdd-5557-511e-b596-d1a1f4a96a8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-167609/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-167609/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-167609/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-167609/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-167609/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-167609/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167609" :question/id #uuid "037afb2b-5a55-553a-97c8-8f8307d403c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-167609" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,1+t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=⟨t,\\,1+t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y=1+t.$    \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t)j \\\\  & =\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t+(1+t)=2t+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+1)\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2t+1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{[{t}^{2}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(1+1-0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-167609/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76447/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "f0f3af21-0544-5039-9d8f-43e4cd5e3a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76447/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "ff0967d0-86e3-51d3-a9f9-24b0f21087d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76447/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "e502bc87-528d-5534-8501-3849a84beb78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76447/selection/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf" :answer/id #uuid "ae5f5a81-6030-592a-bc30-2c070b6f8dd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76447/selection/cadf76b3c9ea81d49a7c0215bbafd960b57c9361c98f1ffb78838a079e98a76e" :answer/id #uuid "8c995502-9a90-584a-8881-7fb8d80be0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76447/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cde44d10-52d3-525f-b78b-6b65b22ba3ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76447/selection/cadf76b3c9ea81d49a7c0215bbafd960b57c9361c98f1ffb78838a079e98a76e" :answer-field/choices ["q-76447/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-76447/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-76447/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-76447/selection/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf" "q-76447/selection/cadf76b3c9ea81d49a7c0215bbafd960b57c9361c98f1ffb78838a079e98a76e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76447" :question/id #uuid "614f2193-cfb2-5440-a30b-e04e95d88a21" :question/math-academy-id "q-76447" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{3}-2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t)=4{t}^{2}\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j$ for $0\\le t\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=4{t}^{2}\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=4{t}^{2}$ and $y=3{t}^{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =8t\\,i+6t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8t)^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{t}^{2}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =10|t| \\\\  & =10t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t>0$ along the path of $C.$ \n\nNow, if $f(x,y)={x}^{3}-2{y}^{3}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={(4{t}^{2})}^{3}-2{(3{t}^{2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}{t}^{6}-2\\cdot {3}^{3}{t}^{6} \\\\  & =64{t}^{6}-54{t}^{6} \\\\  & =10{t}^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{3}-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10{t}^{6}\\cdot 10t\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =100{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{7}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{{t}^{8}}{8}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =100[\\frac{{1}^{8}}{8}+\\frac{{0}^{8}}{8}] \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =12.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76447/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76434/selection/2ba67ff54273661460eaa0e3e45c1c4442f0b6f49f7edadb98be753769c4c9a1" :answer/id #uuid "31314da6-0e2a-5622-b989-f8ce58c41f1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76434/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "a649544b-77aa-59ef-8f08-ec5fc3b21c00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76434/selection/4bd87ad5cdff0b2d0aa7574d5c7450ac33fa34774f895ce16d251ca09a1932ec" :answer/id #uuid "d5c77390-0621-5f80-bee6-3c9b47d9529e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76434/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "7395127b-0dfd-52d8-a4a5-3d32fe835602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76434/selection/df4ef3a75f6d71027299791921d9536d50890079e16123ff435f8ed8ac6150b0" :answer/id #uuid "cc95c043-90dd-5626-a6c1-dfee3e76f56f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76434/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63a227bb-6893-58de-8064-055328e9657e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76434/selection/df4ef3a75f6d71027299791921d9536d50890079e16123ff435f8ed8ac6150b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-76434/selection/2ba67ff54273661460eaa0e3e45c1c4442f0b6f49f7edadb98be753769c4c9a1" "q-76434/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-76434/selection/4bd87ad5cdff0b2d0aa7574d5c7450ac33fa34774f895ce16d251ca09a1932ec" "q-76434/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-76434/selection/df4ef3a75f6d71027299791921d9536d50890079e16123ff435f8ed8ac6150b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76434" :question/id #uuid "d0eae423-33d7-538e-8c9d-ca822c5309ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-76434" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y-x}$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,t-4⟩$ for $t\\in [0,4].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=⟨t,\\,t-4⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y=t-4.$     \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-4)j \\\\  & =i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y-x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{t-(4-t)}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\cdot \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}t\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\cdot (4-0) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76434/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76434"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167621/selection/5bb4db1c5812b970e133d9dfc011cfaef0d6ecf9c044ce03a8abd26a838d839b" :answer/id #uuid "0e409702-08f2-5558-a316-1ec9c707336c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167621/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "0563be26-3310-5716-8a98-8b962611b251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167621/selection/0dcdaba2734e402611268b9f09dc9453bcacd10c2af5095885901c60a71659b9" :answer/id #uuid "76f7b3d4-4461-5267-b4d7-1eab2204cdca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167621/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "1f3fecfc-5d22-5863-a68c-1370aff519d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167621/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "de55a82a-abed-57bd-8980-5c534f56ed54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167621/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "781fa374-acec-5529-b740-2181e55869df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-167621/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer-field/choices ["q-167621/selection/5bb4db1c5812b970e133d9dfc011cfaef0d6ecf9c044ce03a8abd26a838d839b" "q-167621/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-167621/selection/0dcdaba2734e402611268b9f09dc9453bcacd10c2af5095885901c60a71659b9" "q-167621/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" "q-167621/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167621" :question/id #uuid "b61daec6-aad7-5bf4-9c31-4b807b65df11" :question/math-academy-id "q-167621" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}(2{x}^{2}-16)\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$  \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}-16$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-16 \\\\  & =16(2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1) \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(2{x}^{2}-16)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}16\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =64{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =64{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =32[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =32(1-0) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-167621/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167621"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76433/selection/0fc190a80aa55b7e237b98c4a57c0f098e34a998be160b4479cbbfb77cea0d04" :answer/id #uuid "26eb6844-fd82-50d8-9f8f-ea7fe9c06269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi -1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76433/selection/25896a72f5d013c50bb7cb627bf4b333dd1dedb6f0f4e897db2f1ea33bb9ec65" :answer/id #uuid "936b0f98-fdb8-5797-828a-bc1441d4f382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76433/selection/5a7b4531e6893411f5e965bc3c41b80bda4bd86059f58e7aea35f9ae9a2353e8" :answer/id #uuid "2437deb5-8e64-5cbd-905c-e5056bd550db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +2}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76433/selection/e25619b9fd4678c0857c03db9ff03d0f6728d49cd1bc89b3e6b724f4c99172b7" :answer/id #uuid "845e2009-71fa-5b6f-9529-231a18896b04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76433/selection/ad5f441ebc32c9cbb6453f4d59c36a31c9bd747de66abecedf68987450f5cccd" :answer/id #uuid "dc83b966-c6e0-5d92-aeb7-1b45f28b9739" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76433/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f92c8eff-5259-5da6-bddc-821fd3a51c0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76433/selection/25896a72f5d013c50bb7cb627bf4b333dd1dedb6f0f4e897db2f1ea33bb9ec65" :answer-field/choices ["q-76433/selection/0fc190a80aa55b7e237b98c4a57c0f098e34a998be160b4479cbbfb77cea0d04" "q-76433/selection/25896a72f5d013c50bb7cb627bf4b333dd1dedb6f0f4e897db2f1ea33bb9ec65" "q-76433/selection/5a7b4531e6893411f5e965bc3c41b80bda4bd86059f58e7aea35f9ae9a2353e8" "q-76433/selection/e25619b9fd4678c0857c03db9ff03d0f6728d49cd1bc89b3e6b724f4c99172b7" "q-76433/selection/ad5f441ebc32c9cbb6453f4d59c36a31c9bd747de66abecedf68987450f5cccd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76433" :question/id #uuid "3b4075ab-617c-5f07-9e6a-87144b8716f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-76433" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$  \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if $f(x,y)={y}^{2}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}=4{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{[t-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =4[(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2})-0] \\\\  & =\\pi -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76433/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "481a6b6e-05a2-5003-9ac7-b4876ffa4ffa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76433"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76479/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "14f00763-17cb-517e-aa7f-b34d2f22188f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76479/selection/d44fa83f843bb931c0b15366ccb7045f22182cdf2f75578a0b832fc9f01f36a7" :answer/id #uuid "c6efd8f9-ac9b-5e8c-83a1-25e8161c3484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76479/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "91693d11-704e-5413-806f-019bb3f4c9e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76479/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" :answer/id #uuid "2ab6c0c4-5a79-56bb-ba0d-bf8e2cd051d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76479/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "f1c320c4-9342-5cce-8f40-6e49ffb55f47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76479/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad9e170-1fda-541e-b53e-9a87a5e62572" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76479/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer-field/choices ["q-76479/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-76479/selection/d44fa83f843bb931c0b15366ccb7045f22182cdf2f75578a0b832fc9f01f36a7" "q-76479/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-76479/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" "q-76479/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76479" :question/id #uuid "48f8b3e9-e483-5029-956c-3448d88731ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-76479" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$  along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j$ for $0<t<\\sqrt{\\pi /2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}$ and $y=-{t}^{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,j-2t\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}|t| \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ because $t>0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u={t}^{2}$, $\\text{d}u=2t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76479/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da23f1c0-678a-51c0-a2db-e12d756f9120"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76496/selection/5c429644453a56028decff5efc119a2f452c7821852c5bd3171b7bb1b60fa5bc" :answer/id #uuid "d83bd02b-a777-5e2e-8560-b4a08484a40a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}-3\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76496/selection/c2ef053e54c718f9bf1d1c302c5ba1c1a990d982b6662b20659cd49e09038e1e" :answer/id #uuid "0fc32d82-883e-5d9a-9ef6-fda78b8edef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76496/selection/ff86b8eac983f515b0113e993d7ec60d46a3ea866ab258ea2b303f8e416f7470" :answer/id #uuid "3c8fc1b6-450d-59c4-b7d1-94d412236028" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}-3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76496/selection/851635c60b7fd189e93d1da05f0b1d7093b8fafaaf7c5967bc78a98f5a259d88" :answer/id #uuid "06649df6-d0e6-5c19-b0bf-811b6d16991b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76496/selection/0e0062fa945712a42676599e7838765ddd8a099e340b0ff4426c5a13dd091503" :answer/id #uuid "ec8bde36-aa42-53ec-8a9d-c7fd1d226bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76496/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "162e39cd-8ff0-5480-8347-cac99e7301ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76496/selection/5c429644453a56028decff5efc119a2f452c7821852c5bd3171b7bb1b60fa5bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-76496/selection/5c429644453a56028decff5efc119a2f452c7821852c5bd3171b7bb1b60fa5bc" "q-76496/selection/c2ef053e54c718f9bf1d1c302c5ba1c1a990d982b6662b20659cd49e09038e1e" "q-76496/selection/ff86b8eac983f515b0113e993d7ec60d46a3ea866ab258ea2b303f8e416f7470" "q-76496/selection/851635c60b7fd189e93d1da05f0b1d7093b8fafaaf7c5967bc78a98f5a259d88" "q-76496/selection/0e0062fa945712a42676599e7838765ddd8a099e340b0ff4426c5a13dd091503"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76496" :question/id #uuid "3ae3502e-bab7-5151-a4d7-a87bc90c161b" :question/math-academy-id "q-76496" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{y+z}{x}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,j+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,k$\nfor $1<t<\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=t\\,i+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,j+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,k,$ then along the curve we have $x=t,$ $y=\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},$ and $z=\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})\\,k \\\\  & =i+t\\,j+t\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=\\frac{y+z}{x}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}}{t}=t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{y+z}{x}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+2{t}^{2}$, $\\text{d}u=4t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({5}^{3/2}-{3}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}-3\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-76496/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da23f1c0-678a-51c0-a2db-e12d756f9120"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167612/selection/6a3ffee1363d2c3064ca56944b635781c360776ae17ebb1420224ca59708f456" :answer/id #uuid "4e9679eb-4863-51a3-9ba7-bf6a9c13b48c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14(2\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167612/selection/8a6a9df3a8f8456c0503063f020c6643232c090de07f9eaad5a607f753bd9f76" :answer/id #uuid "f752b4fe-a04b-50da-b02e-d61483613bcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7(2\\sqrt{2}+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167612/selection/c70cc94404ccb83814bc96b6dfe35ea982ac823a50f73679b07eb5cc5d5092e4" :answer/id #uuid "06632d28-6287-5b07-9284-f75c44dbc8b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167612/selection/e65285ef5a76c8887526a5e3fdd1695e46c64662e742881e60197e7d0fc0c72c" :answer/id #uuid "73f5d0dd-bc57-52d6-adac-712951acca42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{2}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167612/selection/f7dca4479b026383a17a4b72e994fa3d1ef9bbd6ec5c7f9c9a847634cbfe8185" :answer/id #uuid "acc14017-54b2-56d9-a74e-f25a9d097346" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167612/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "96fee648-e37b-5595-ae19-12b280cdc426" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-167612/selection/6a3ffee1363d2c3064ca56944b635781c360776ae17ebb1420224ca59708f456" :answer-field/choices ["q-167612/selection/6a3ffee1363d2c3064ca56944b635781c360776ae17ebb1420224ca59708f456" "q-167612/selection/8a6a9df3a8f8456c0503063f020c6643232c090de07f9eaad5a607f753bd9f76" "q-167612/selection/c70cc94404ccb83814bc96b6dfe35ea982ac823a50f73679b07eb5cc5d5092e4" "q-167612/selection/e65285ef5a76c8887526a5e3fdd1695e46c64662e742881e60197e7d0fc0c72c" "q-167612/selection/f7dca4479b026383a17a4b72e994fa3d1ef9bbd6ec5c7f9c9a847634cbfe8185"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167612" :question/id #uuid "94613a61-5d6f-54bc-ad9b-93f7bd953468" :question/math-academy-id "q-167612" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=3t\\,i+{t}^{3}\\,j\\,$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=3t\\,i+{t}^{3}\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=3t$ and $y={t}^{3}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,j \\\\  & =3\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{(3{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3t)^{3}+{t}^{3} \\\\  & =27{t}^{3}+{t}^{3} \\\\  & =28{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}28{t}^{3}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}84{t}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+{t}^{4},$ $\\text{d}u=4{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}84{t}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}21\\cdot {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =14({2}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =14(2\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-167612/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da23f1c0-678a-51c0-a2db-e12d756f9120"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-76186"] :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{12x}{y-1}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t+1)\\,j\\,$ for $t\\in [\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{6}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t+1)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}$ and $y=t+1.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{12x}{y-1}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{12{t}^{2}}{(t+1)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12{t}^{2}}{t} \\\\  & =12t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}12t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4{t}^{2}+1,$ $\\text{d}u=8t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}12t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{9}^{25}\\frac{3}{2}{u}^{1/2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{3/2}{|}_{9}^{25} \\\\  & ={25}^{3/2}-{9}^{3/2} \\\\  & =125-27 \\\\  & =98\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-76484/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "e228621b-8850-5ac9-b53c-670a8bfd641f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76484/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "9d5567ca-58a0-5b55-ae41-49bc9ab41b10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76484/selection/4ca7e04cb32d17c1971e27f96c827d785e809ee86fbe2e04813f39f29bdc8cde" :answer/id #uuid "356f73a7-55ab-5999-8ccd-70972a9a9763" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76484/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" :answer/id #uuid "f93a92a5-7142-5e27-98a4-94f99cb7ca17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76484/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "e5cf0cd7-cb38-52f5-9b33-7dfdce43acd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76484/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f98bb9d-7cd2-51d1-bc92-804e8c3bc811" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76484/selection/4ca7e04cb32d17c1971e27f96c827d785e809ee86fbe2e04813f39f29bdc8cde" :answer-field/choices ["q-76484/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-76484/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-76484/selection/4ca7e04cb32d17c1971e27f96c827d785e809ee86fbe2e04813f39f29bdc8cde" "q-76484/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" "q-76484/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76484" :question/id #uuid "0a87a0d6-612c-52cc-a302-217bb9a4cf9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76484" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{5},$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ and $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$   \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =5|\\operatorname{cos}⁡t| \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\ge 0$ when $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{5}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{25{sin}^{2}⁡t}{5} \\\\  & =5{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}5{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =25{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =25{\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =25\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =25(\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76484/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da23f1c0-678a-51c0-a2db-e12d756f9120"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76484"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6307"] :question/problem "Find an integral that is equivalent to $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_C xy^3 \\, \\textrm{d}s,$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf r(t)= \\left \\langle \\cos t, \\sin t \\right\\rangle$ for $t \\in \\left(0, \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053150/assets/f53d78debfec5f8c50e0f3a5947d2a36126e18c073d7b0cc4c59d506753059b3.png)\n\nThe path of integration is shown above. We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we have $f(x,y) =  xy^3$. Along the path, we have $x=\\cos t$ and $y=\\sin t,$ and so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =f(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{3} \\\\  & ={sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C xy^3 \\, \\textrm{d}s = \\int^{\\pi/2}_{0} \\sin^3 t \\cos t \\, \\textrm{d}t .\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6308"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_{C}xy\\,\\textrm{d}s,$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t) = 3t\\,\\mathbf{i}+4t\\,\\mathbf{j}\\,$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t) = 3t\\,\\mathbf{i}+4t\\,\\mathbf{j},$ then along the curve we have $x=3t$ and $y=4t.$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y) =xy,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3t\\cdot 4t \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}12{t}^{2}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =60{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =60{[\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =20{[{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6283"] :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of $f(x,y,z) = \\dfrac{x}{yz}$ along the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t) = t^2\\, \\mathbf{i} + t \\,\\mathbf{j} + 1 \\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t \\in [0,\\sqrt 2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t) =t^2\\, \\mathbf{i} + t \\,\\mathbf{j} + 1 \\,\\mathbf{k},$ then along the curve we have $x = t^2,$ $y = t,$ and $z=1.$  \n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+1\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z) = \\dfrac{x}{yz},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{t\\cdot 1}=t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u= 4t^2+1,$ $\\textrm d u=8t\\,\\textrm d t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{8}{u}^{1/2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[{9}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[27-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 26 \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
